	('799dfd37-65d1-443c-be84-492184a5ee34', '22443ea6-1955-4fab-abca-1ff36da9a308', 'Operator, Armoring Machine', 'We
are proud to offer competitive compensation, employee benefits, tuition reimbursement and unlimited growth opportunities. Our more than seven decades of progressive growth can be attributed to our determination to developing innovative systems and solutions, exercising environmental stewardship and enhancing the well-being of the communities in which we work and live. How will you power what’s possible?
Location: MC - Carrollton, GA
Shift: D: 6:50p-7a
Pay Rate: 27.40 - 29.16
The Operator, Armoring, is a medium skill role will process steel/aluminum MC Cable to achieve safety, quality and efficiency requirements. Initial duties will include but are not limited to loading and unloading raw material and correctly tagging material.
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS:
High school diploma or equivalent
Must read, write, and speak English; Bilingual in Spanish is a plus
Must be able to stand and lift heavy loads for long periods of time
Operator must be able lift up to 45 lbs
Operator must be able to follow instructions
Operator must be able to interpret production orders
Any other job duties as assigned
PRIMARY JOB TASKS:
Operator should be training to qualify in the operation, coordinating several tasks in such a manner to maximize production while safely maintaining specific procedures and quality of steel/aluminum MC Cable
Operator must learn to make judgements concerning quality of the steel/aluminum MC Cable
Operator will learn to interact with computer controls to operate machine/work cell
Operator will learn to interact with control panels to pinpoint and eliminate various operating problems
Operator will learn to coordinate material handling, production with other operators on the line to ensure a continuous production process
Operator will learn to maintain material levels for all levels of operation
Operator will be responsible for loading and unloading of raw materials and finished goods
Must be able to work under supervision and maintain ongoing communication with the supervisor and peers through verbal instruction and reports
Identify scrap and place into designated scrap areas
CROSS TRAINING:
Will be required to cross-train on equipment within your identified workgroup at your facility
Once trained in more complex jobs, may be required to fill the position in the event of absence or vacancy
Will be required to rotate on a set frequency within your workgroup to maintain skill proficiency
QUALITY:
Use the company’s ISO Quality System documentation to help guide all daily quality activities
Do not release products until all quality checks have been passed
Immediately report quality issues to the supervisor, department manager, or quality manager
SAFETY:
Working safely is a condition of employment
Follow all company environmental rules/procedures and handle all materials in a manner designed to minimize environmental impact
Follow all safety procedures and rules including safe material handling
Properly wear all required PPE
Review and know all Job Hazard Analyses for proper job sequence and hazards associated with the jobs assigned to do
Review and know all Safety Data Sheets for the jobs assigned to do
Maintain all work areas to 5S standards
Perform pre-operation safety inspection and hazard analysis
Responsible to observe Southwire safety rules and maintain good housekeeping
PHYSICAL/ENVIRONMENTAL DEMANDS:
Physical activity associated with daily performance of this job include: balance, climbing, fingering, grasping, hearing, kneeling, lifting, pulling, pushing, reaching, repetitive motions, standing, stooping, walking and sitting
Must be able to work in hot and cold environments normally found in a prefabricated building without climate-control
Operator may be exposed to high levels of noise and a dusty environment
Operator may be exposed to gaseous lift fumes
Operator may be exposed to hazardous material', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '9abcbdd3-8991-46e4-9024-97e25045a8f9', 'Carrollton', 'GA', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-30', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', 'https://careers.southwire.com/job/Carrollton-Operator%2C-Armoring-Machine-GA-30119/1395615900/', 'southwire', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00'),
	('a7e40be5-b16b-402f-9c30-284ce409cdd9', '22443ea6-1955-4fab-abca-1ff36da9a308', 'Extruder Operator', 'We
are proud to offer competitive compensation, employee benefits, tuition reimbursement and unlimited growth opportunities. Our more than seven decades of progressive growth can be attributed to our determination to developing innovative systems and solutions, exercising environmental stewardship and enhancing the well-being of the communities in which we work and live. How will you power what’s possible?
Location: BREMENEAST
Shift: TBD
Pay Rate: $27.12 – $30.69
The Extruder Operator is a high skill role that will set up and operate extrusion lines and related equipment, including nylon extruders, pay-offs and take-ups. These lines that fall under this job class mainly operate as two person lines.
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS:
High school diploma or equivalent
Must be able to stand and lift heavy loads for long periods of time
Must be able to read and comprehend production orders and the instrumentation on complex equipment
Must be able to lift up to 45 lbs
Basic math skills (adding, subtracting, etc..)
Judgments concerning operation of extrusion line and related equipment are encountered
PRIMARY JOB TASKS:
Must be able to work under supervision and maintain ongoing communication with the supervisor and peers through verbal instruction and reports
Put scrap into the designated scrap bins
Responsible for proper setup of extrusion line and related equipment with correct tip and die and correct wire size
Responsible to maintain correct wire size, insulation thickness and concentricity
Responsible for application of correct print of acceptable quality on cable
Responsible to observe Southwire safety rules, maintain good housekeeping and perform all other duties as assigned
Responsible for using proper compound and correct amounts of color concentrate
Responsible to keep wire and compound loss at a minimum during start-up and changeovers
Responsible for correct inventory of WIP tags daily
CROSS TRAINING:
Will be required to cross-train on equipment within your identified workgroup at your facility
Once trained in more complex jobs, may be required to fill the position in the event of absence or vacancy
Will be required to rotate on a set frequency within your workgroup to maintain skill proficiency
QUALITY:
Use the company’s ISO Quality System documentation to help guide all daily quality activities
Do not release products until all quality checks have been passed
Immediately report quality issues to the supervisor or quality manager
SAFETY:
Working safely is a condition of employment
Follow all company environmental rules/procedures and handle all materials in a manner designed to minimize environmental impact
Extruders give off a substantial amount of radiant heat
The hopper vacuums, motors, air-wipes and other machinery can be quite noisy
Properly wear all required PPE
Review and know all Job Hazard Analyses for proper job sequence and hazards associated with the jobs assigned to do
Review and know all Safety Data Sheets for the jobs assigned to do
Maintain all work areas to 5S standards
Perform pre-operation safety inspection and hazard analysis
PHYSICAL/ENVIRONMENTAL DEMANDS:
Physical activity associated with daily performance of this job include: balance, climbing, fingering, grasping, hearing, kneeling, lifting, pulling, pushing, reaching, repetitive motions, standing, stooping, walking and sitting
Must be able to work in hot and cold environments normally found in a prefabricated building without climate-control
The operator is constantly exposed to water, some heat, cold, dust and fumes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '9abcbdd3-8991-46e4-9024-97e25045a8f9', 'Bremen', 'IN', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '$27.12 – $30.69', '{}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-30', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', 'https://careers.southwire.com/job/Bremen-Extruder-Operator-IN-46506/1395641300/', 'southwire', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00'),
	('9078a080-a182-482f-ad58-652cb90d23a4', '22443ea6-1955-4fab-abca-1ff36da9a308', 'Lineman', 'Location: Remote
Shift: 7am-4pm
Starting Pay Rate: $42.00
This position is responsible for the safe repair and rejuvenation of medium to high voltage underground cables using Novinium’s patented technology and processes.', 'Relevant work experience as a Lineman, Class A Lineman, Class B Lineman, First Class Power Lineman, or Cable Splicer with current certification or documentation
Experience with underground line work, including URD, fault location and repair, and switching
Strong Lineman underground craftwork skills, including inline splices, terminations and elbows
Ability to read circuit maps
Basic computer skills and entry level proficiency with MS Office applications (Outlook, Word, Excel, internet/web)
Understanding of basic construction skills
Strong mechanical skills
Familiarity with URD systems and cables, fault repair and switching
Safe work record and a firm commitment to safety
Valid driver’s license and acceptable DMV record
CDL preferred
Passport and ability to travel to Canada preferred
Working Conditions
Able and willing to travel on a regular basis
Able to safely climb poles if needed
Able to lift, push, pull and carry at least 75 lbs. for a distance of 300 ft.
Able to stand, kneel and work in confined spaces for an extended period of time
Must be able to fit into a confined space rescue harness
Must conduct digging operations as required
Frequent sitting, standing and walking
Frequent exposure to seasonal elements
Conditions may vary based on assignment', NULL, 'Safety
Work safely with no electrical contact incidents or personal injuries
Enhance and advance a below zero incident safety culture and behavior
Comprehend and follow OSHA and company safety rules
Responsible for the safety of all people at a worksite
Craftwork
Operate TDR  waveform and RF locating equipment to perform cable testing and analysis of cable paths, splice locations and neutral corrosion
Place and operate cable injection equipment on de-energized and energized cables in transformers, switchgear, junction boxes and at other cable end points
Perform air flow tests
Prepare cable for injection activities, including electrical craftwork according to quality standards
Inject URD and feeder cables with Novinium patented repair/rejuvenation fluids using sustained and un-sustained rejuvenation technologies
Provide field service and set up injection equipment
Switch medium voltage electrical circuits
Write and implement cable switching orders, manage switching contact with circuit owner
Climb poles to perform work if needed
Carry out other duties as assigned
Project Management
May coordinate injection and digging activities (competency in excavation)
Maintain rolling stock and equipment
Select Injection Adapters, and cable accessories
Assist Team Leader with job planning, hazard avoidance, and recording daily work records
Operate company vehicles and equipment, including bucket trucks, as required
Customer Relations
Provide positive customer service', NULL, 'ecc0ecfc-6c93-4c15-8855-0f43a71cb82f', 'Miami', 'FL', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '$42.00', '{}', '{}', NULL, 'entry', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-29', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', 'https://careers.southwire.com/job/Miami-Lineman-FL-33186/1181618600/', 'southwire', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00'),
	('ba15d1ca-d836-4150-95d0-4d5829378ff1', '22443ea6-1955-4fab-abca-1ff36da9a308', 'Electrician - Sr. Electronic Technician', 'We
are proud to offer competitive compensation, employee benefits, tuition reimbursement and unlimited growth opportunities. Our more than seven decades of progressive growth can be attributed to our determination to developing innovative systems and solutions, exercising environmental stewardship and enhancing the well-being of the communities in which we work and live. How will you power what’s possible?
Location: Hawesville, KY
Shift: 12 hour
Pay Rate: $35.25 – $39.68
Candidates who are selected will be eligible to qualify for the Sr Electronic Technician position, which offers a pay rate of $42.50
GENERAL SUMMARY:
Under the direction of the supervisor, an individual will be expected to troubleshoot, disassemble, repair, assemble, install, relocate or modify complex electrical equipment.
PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:
1.    Troubleshoot and repair, install or modify complicated relay logic systems, circuit breakers, fuses, transformers, motors, lighting systems, switches, bus ducts and high voltage power distribution systems.
2.    Install hardware portion of programmable controllers.  Troubleshoot hardware and program using the programming terminal.
3.    Select and use applicable tools and materials to accomplish assigned tasks in an efficient and safe manner.
4.    Perform assigned tasks with input from supervisor, maintenance work order, machine operator and maintenance manuals.
5.    Complete all forms as required by management, including but not limited to:  maintenance work orders, inspection reports, and P.M. check lists using hard copy and/or computer generated forms.
6.    Must handle all materials in a manner designed to minimize environmental impact.
SKILLS AND ABILITIES
1.    Must be able to satisfactorily complete certification program for "Senior" Electrician.
2.    Thorough knowledge of, and ability to correctly use, all hand tools, power tools and precision measuring instruments.
3.    Ability to select all tools, parts and materials to complete assigned tasks.
4.    Ability to lead and work with a small crew.
5.    Ability to read and interpret complicated lighting and power distribution drawings and relay logic schematics.
6.    Ability to install complicated conduit systems.
WORKING CONDITIONS:
Could be exposed to working conditions such as inclement weather, heat, cold, noise, vibration, dust, dirt, fumes, water, oil and heights.  Where conditions require, protective equipment will be issued to the employee.
EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE:
High school diploma or equivalent is required.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ecc0ecfc-6c93-4c15-8855-0f43a71cb82f', 'Hawesville', 'KY', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '$35.25 – $39.68', '{}', '{}', NULL, 'senior', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-28', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', 'https://careers.southwire.com/job/Hawesville-Electrician-Sr_-Electronic-Technician-KY-42348/1403896600/', 'southwire', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00'),
	('1bf0ac7a-e529-4e85-9cdb-5bea8e082fd1', '22443ea6-1955-4fab-abca-1ff36da9a308', 'Electronic Technician', 'As a Electronic Technician, you will support our manufacturing operations by providing a full range of electronic equipment maintenance with focus on reliability. Ensure sustainable operation of machinery and equipment by completing preventive maintenance requirements on motors, conveyor systems, and other production machinery. The Electronic Technician will also be a key member of process improvement and problem-solving teams.
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS:
High school graduate or equivalent is required. Technical degree preferred.
Strong electronic background
Must have computer skills (Microsoft Office, CMMS, Excel, etc.)
Ability to interpret technical drawings, schematics and OEM manuals.
Understand manufacturing processes and manufacturing equipment.
Must be familiar with normal test equipment such as multimeters/oscilloscopes.
Ability to read and interpret precision measuring devices.
Must be capable of handling multiple tasks simultaneously.
Ability to work in a high speed, fast-paced environment.
Must pass written and hands-on certification tests.
PRIMARY JOB TASKS:
Troubleshoot equipment malfunctions using logical and systematic methodologies.
Routine maintenance including but not limited to field fault analysis, calibration of instrumentation using proper test equipment, component replacement, alignment and calibration to specification.
Troubleshoot and repair various equipment to include electronic, digital equipment and AC/DC motors & controls.
Fault analysis of hard-wired relay logic, motor control circuits, motor power circuits (single & 3 phase) and common utility/lighting circuits.
Access and use PLC logic programming to troubleshoot production equipment.
Replacement of identified failed parts or components.
Adjust equipment to bring it into operational specifications.
Recommend process or procedure changes based on observed equipment behavior.
Testing of electrical systems and continuity of circuits in electrical wiring, using testing devices such as ohmmeters, and voltmeters to ensure proper operation and safety of system.
Install, examine, replace or repair electrical wiring, receptacles, switch boxes, conduits, lighting fixtures and other electrical components.
Maintain current and accurate maintenance data to determine establish historical records and future maintenance requirements.
QUALITY:
Maintain an attitude of learning to stay current with maintenance procedures and equipment.
Complete annual Maintenance Skills Assessment
SAFETY:
Report all accidents, incidents, injuries and unsafe acts or conditions, immediately to the supervisor.
Must follow prescribed safety procedures to prevent injury and maintain safe equipment and conditions in entire plant.
PHYSICAL/ENVIRONMENTAL DEMANDS:
Ability to meet the physical requirements of working safely in an industrial maintenance environment.
Follow all company environmental rules/procedures and handle all materials in a manner designed to minimize environmental impact.
Southwire is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ecc0ecfc-6c93-4c15-8855-0f43a71cb82f', 'Carrollton', 'GA', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-27', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', 'https://careers.southwire.com/job/Carrollton-Electronic-Technician-GA-30117/1395138000/', 'southwire', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00'),
	('c59fb581-b5f9-468d-b2fb-c51061d01155', '22443ea6-1955-4fab-abca-1ff36da9a308', 'Apprentice, Machinist', 'We
are proud to offer competitive compensation, employee benefits, tuition reimbursement and unlimited growth opportunities. Our more than seven decades of progressive growth can be attributed to our determination to developing innovative systems and solutions, exercising environmental stewardship and enhancing the well-being of the communities in which we work and live. How will you power what’s possible?
Location: MC and MSG
Shift: 7a-3p M-Fr
Pay Rate: $23.90 – $23.90
Job Summary/Objective:
The Machinist Apprenticeship Program provides a pathway for individuals to learn and master CNC Machining skills while earning a salary in a career that can lead to opportunities and advancement within the manufacturing industry.
As a student and apprentice, you will rotate between attending classes and working at Southwire. Upon successful completion of the apprenticeship program, you will be equipped with both hands-on and institutional knowledge of Machining and will be prepared be to assume a role as Machinist II.
Southwire Machinist Apprenticeship Program includes the following commitments from you:
•    The Machinist Apprenticeship Program requires a 2-year commitment to work and school.
•    The ability to apply for technical school financial aid for applicable grants, scholarships prior to acceptance into the program.', NULL, NULL, 'Here is our commitment to you:
•    The ability to get paid to go to school & work immediately.
•    Experience hands-on instruction.
•    Apply your new skills to real projects for Southwire.
•    Learn from lead instructors and industry professionals.
•    Competitive wages that are line with the program. Periodic pay increases based upon successful completion of both classroom training and on the job tasks.
•    Comprehensive benefits program which includes medical, dental, prescription, and life insurance, as well as 401K and time off benefits.', NULL, '9abcbdd3-8991-46e4-9024-97e25045a8f9', 'Carrollton', 'GA', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '$23.90 – $23.90', '{}', '{}', NULL, 'senior', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-27', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00', 'https://careers.southwire.com/job/Carrollton-Apprentice%2C-Machinist-GA-30117/1395080100/', 'southwire', '2026-06-30 22:37:20.0636+00'),
