 operate, and ‘inclusion’ is one of our core values. We believe our differences make us stronger as a company and as individuals and we are committed to championing inclusivity in everything we do. At Schneider Electric, we uphold the highest standards of ethics and compliance, and we believe that trust is a foundational value. Our Trust Charter is our Code of Conduct and demonstrates our commitment to ethics, safety, sustainability, quality and cybersecurity, underpinning every aspect of our business and our willingness to behave and respond respectfully and in good faith to all our stakeholders. You can find out more about our Trust Charter here Schneider Electric is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is our policy to provide equal employment and advancement opportunities in the areas of recruiting, hiring, training, transferring, and promoting all qualified individuals regardless of race, religion, color, gender, disability, national origin, ancestry, age, military status, sexual orientation, marital status, or any other legally protected characteristic or conduct.', NULL, 'SKILLS & ABILITIES: Advanced understanding of HVAC, access or other building or electronic control systems Intermediate ability to use Microsoft Office programs including but not limited to, Word, Excel and PowerPoint EDUCATION: Two-year (2) degree in a related technical field required or related work experience   EXPERIENCE: Four years related work experience required Knowledge of video surveillance and access control systems a plus Schneider Electric also offers a comprehensive benefits package to support our employees, inclusive of medical (with member reward points), dental, vision, and basic life insurance, Benefit Bucks (credits to apply towards your benefits) flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, 401(k) + match, well-being and recognition (including service anniversary) programs, 12 holidays per year, 15 days of paid time off per year (pro-rated in the first year of employment based on start date), opportunity to purchase company stock (eligibility depends on start date), and military leave benefits. You must submit an online application to be considered for any position with us. This position will be posted until filled.', 'Schneider Electric has an opportunity for a Building Automation Service Specialist II in our Las Vegas, NV location.  This position will allow you to be a part of an inclusive team, the opportunity to be hands on and customer facing.  What do you get to do in this position?  Software experience is a plus to perform controls sequence modifications. Protocols: LonWorks and/or BACnet (INET, VISTA, CONTINUUM, I/A, Eco-Struxure is a plus) Performs commissioning of control systems to ensure proper operation Repair and reconfigure control system equipment, including conduit, wire and field devices Diagnose communication problems and install control devices and other components Diagnose and troubleshoot software and hardware issues Troubleshoot and verify correct operation of equipment and field devices Install, replace and re-commission devices, equipment and software Assist in performing job site training sessions Develop graphics and custom list views Oversees subcontractors to meet specifications and schedule Provides emergency and warranty service as required May lead project installation team in executing systems installations Provide technical support to other team members Troubleshooting video surveillance and access control systems Other duties may be assigned', NULL, '40b56afc-87b9-4e70-94fc-e5bc65a2a21c', 'Las Vegas', 'NV', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, 'Experienced', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-03-02', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', 'https://careers.se.com/jobs/110760', 'schneider_electric', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00'),
	('d6385f00-ebab-4361-80de-2df840a3fb5c', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'In Process Quality Technician - 1st Shift', 'Schneider Electric is seeking an In Process Quality Technician for incoming inspection on 1st shift to join our team in Mt Juliet, TN. If you have a strong background in testing low and medium voltage products, coupled with the ability to collaborate closely with Engineering, we want to hear from you. What will your responsibilities be? Perform detailed inspections of incoming components and materials to verify compliance with specifications and quality standards. Identify, document, and escalate non-conformances; collaborate with internal teams to resolve quality issues promptly. Ensure adherence to company quality procedures, safety guidelines, and industry standards during all inspection activities. Work closely with production, engineering, and supply chain teams to maintain smooth workflow and uphold quality expectations. Accurately record inspection results in SAP and maintain proper documentation for traceability and audits. Wear prescribed Personal Protective Equipment and maintain it in good condition. Immediately report hazards, incidents, and accidents to supervisors. Adhere to Provincial HS&E legislation, regulations, and company policies. High school diploma or GED required. Must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. without company sponsorship and able to pass a pre-employment drug screen and background check. Skilled in validating and correcting technical documents, including test procedures. Able to manage technical tasks independently with strong analytical skills and the ability to interpret schematics. Effective communicator with exceptional interpersonal skills (written and oral), strong organizational abilities, and computer proficiency. Basic Requirements: PPE (Personal Protective Equipment) is required; safety shoes and safety glasses must be worn on the production floor Work is performed in a Manufacturing Environment, where prolonged period(s) of standing is required for duration of shift. Requires ability to reach overhead, pull, push, bend, squat, and climb a ladder to perform work. Ability to lift 26 pounds occasionally or 22 pounds independently and repetitively. What''s in it for me? Competitive pay & annual Pay for Performance structure. Opportunity for Overtime pay PLUS shift differential Medical, Dental, Vision plan effective on day one. Paid Holidays, Paid Time Off Paid primary and secondary paid parental leave including adoption 401(k) Match Employee Assistance Program and Wellness Program and more For this U.S. based position, the expected compensation range is $19.30-$28.90 per hour. In addition, this position is eligible for overtime pay and may also include premium pay or differentials, depending on location. The compensation rate for this position is for candidates located within the United States. Individual pay is determined by several factors including knowledge, job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. The compensation range for this full-time position applies to candidates located within the United States. Our salary ranges are determined by reviewing roles of similar responsibility and level. Within the salary range, individual pay is determined by several factors including performance, knowledge, job related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Schneider Electric also offers a comprehensive benefits package to support our employees, inclusive of medical, (with member reward points), dental, vision, and basic life insurance, Benefit Bucks (credits to apply towards your benefits), flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, 401(k) + match, well-being programs and recognition (including service anniversary), 12 holidays per year, 15 days of paid time off per year (pro-rated in the first year of employment based on start date), opportunity to purchase company stock (eligibility depends on start date), and military leave benefits. You must submit an online application to be considered for the position. The Company will accept applications on an ongoing basis until the position is filled.', NULL, 'High school diploma or GED required. Must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. without company sponsorship and able to pass a pre-employment drug screen and background check. Skilled in validating and correcting technical documents, including test procedures. Able to manage technical tasks independently with strong analytical skills and the ability to interpret schematics. Effective communicator with exceptional interpersonal skills (written and oral), strong organizational abilities, and computer proficiency. Basic Requirements: PPE (Personal Protective Equipment) is required; safety shoes and safety glasses must be worn on the production floor Work is performed in a Manufacturing Environment, where prolonged period(s) of standing is required for duration of shift. Requires ability to reach overhead, pull, push, bend, squat, and climb a ladder to perform work. Ability to lift 26 pounds occasionally or 22 pounds independently and repetitively. What''s in it for me? Competitive pay & annual Pay for Performance structure. Opportunity for Overtime pay PLUS shift differential Medical, Dental, Vision plan effective on day one. Paid Holidays, Paid Time Off Paid primary and secondary paid parental leave including adoption 401(k) Match Employee Assistance Program and Wellness Program and more For this U.S. based position, the expected compensation range is $19.30-$28.90 per hour. In addition, this position is eligible for overtime pay and may also include premium pay or differentials, depending on location. The compensation rate for this position is for candidates located within the United States. Individual pay is determined by several factors including knowledge, job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. The compensation range for this full-time position applies to candidates located within the United States. Our salary ranges are determined by reviewing roles of similar responsibility and level. Within the salary range, individual pay is determined by several factors including performance, knowledge, job related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Schneider Electric also offers a comprehensive benefits package to support our employees, inclusive of medical, (with member reward points), dental, vision, and basic life insurance, Benefit Bucks (credits to apply towards your benefits), flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, 401(k) + match, well-being programs and recognition (including service anniversary), 12 holidays per year, 15 days of paid time off per year (pro-rated in the first year of employment based on start date), opportunity to purchase company stock (eligibility depends on start date), and military leave benefits. You must submit an online application to be considered for the position. The Company will accept applications on an ongoing basis until the position is filled.', 'Schneider Electric is seeking an In Process Quality Technician for incoming inspection on 1st shift to join our team in Mt Juliet, TN. If you have a strong background in testing low and medium voltage products, coupled with the ability to collaborate closely with Engineering, we want to hear from you. What will your responsibilities be? Perform detailed inspections of incoming components and materials to verify compliance with specifications and quality standards. Identify, document, and escalate non-conformances; collaborate with internal teams to resolve quality issues promptly. Ensure adherence to company quality procedures, safety guidelines, and industry standards during all inspection activities. Work closely with production, engineering, and supply chain teams to maintain smooth workflow and uphold quality expectations. Accurately record inspection results in SAP and maintain proper documentation for traceability and audits. Wear prescribed Personal Protective Equipment and maintain it in good condition. Immediately report hazards, incidents, and accidents to supervisors. Adhere to Provincial HS&E legislation, regulations, and company policies.', NULL, '9abcbdd3-8991-46e4-9024-97e25045a8f9', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '$19.30-$28.90 per hour', '{}', '{}', NULL, 'Experienced', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-30', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', 'https://careers.se.com/jobs/125172', 'schneider_electric', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00'),
	('016d47a9-76ee-451b-9fc4-3bcff80c0d91', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Material Associate II', '1st Shift Role This position is responsible for the routine and advanced material handling responsibilities within a product line. Responsible for maintaining adequate inventory levels to ensure maximum productivity of workers. SKILL (Education, Experience, Initiative, and Ingenuity) High School Education or GED required 3-5 years’ experience in material handling function Ability to work independently Uses independent judgement and initiative to resolve supply problems, consulting supervisor only when all options have been exhausted May be required to have forklift certification SAP experience is a plus Must be able to read and understand blueprint/material drawings Basic computer knowledge required EFFORT (Physical Demand, Mental or Visual Demand) Job cannot be performed alternating sitting and standing Requires ability to use hand and foot controls Requires ability to reach overhead, lift up to 26 pounds, and be on feet for long hours, stooping, bending, pulling and pushing Proper use of various lifting devices required. Requires ability to reach overhead, pull, push, and climb a ladder to perform work. RESPONSIBILITY (Equipment or Process, Material or Product, Safety of Others, Work of Others) Responsible for the continuous supply of materials to one or more production or assembly areas Responsible for “kitting” materials on the production line to ensure all parts of order required are at point of origination to keep line moving at steady pace Responsible for picking parts from Kanban or storage areas and placing the parts into a storage bin (kit) Ensures correct parts are kept in the appropriate quantities to support production and assembly requirements May take parts from inventory area and ensures Water Spider is kept stocked at appropriate levels of inventory Performs repetitive and advanced material supply functions following detailed work direction and guidelines May operate forklift truck or hand truck for delivery or picking of parts and supplies Sorts and counts parts and supplies and logs inventory Inspects parts for damages or defects; records discrepancies or damages and notifies supervisor and/or purchasing personnel Expedites parts and uses independent judgement to resolve part shortages May trace or track lost parts and supplies Regularly interacts with production assemblers and testers May maintain department database, prepare routine reports, and file kitter records Document material movement using computer tablets Responsible for rotating KB material FIFO Material audits, turning in and documenting KB cards for replenishment Follows established departmental policies, procedures, and objectives, continuous quality improvement objectives, and safety, environmental, and/or infection control standards Document proper care in the use and maintenance of equipment and supplies; promotes continuous improvement of workplace safety and environmental practices Establishes and maintains a safe and healthful working environment in accordance with OSHA requirements Performs other tasks as may be requested to assure the effective and continuous utilization of assets JOB CONDITIONS (Working Conditions, Hazards) Safety shoes and safety glasses are required. Work is performed in a manufacturing and assembly line environment. If material handling equipment is not operated properly, injury could result to self or others. What''s in it for me? (add additional benefits specific to job here) Who will you report to? Let us learn about you! Apply today. Looking to make an IMPACT with your career? When you are thinking about joining a new team, culture matters. At Schneider Electric, our values and behaviors are the foundation for creating a great culture to support business success. We believe that our IMPACT values – Inclusion, Mastery, Purpose, Action, Curiosity, Teamwork – starts with us. IMPACT is also your invitation to