	('59912a47-216a-452d-bb8b-8a4bb446c398', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Warehouse Operator (2nd Shift)', 'Join our warehouse team and become part of a supply chain that delivers results every day. We''re hiring a Warehouse Operations Operator who''s ready to roll up their sleeves, work safely, and help us fulfill orders with accuracy and efficiency. What will you do? Handle receiving, storing, and shipping tasks to ensure timely and accurate order fulfillment Organize and maintain inventory while supporting proper stock rotation and product quality Operate warehouse equipment safely and follow all operational and safety procedures Collaborate with team members to meet daily productivity goals and maintain a clean, efficient workspace What are the key skills we are looking for? Continuous Improvement — developing level; identifying opportunities to streamline warehouse processes and reduce inefficiencies Customer Orientation — developing level; ensuring orders are fulfilled accurately and on time to meet customer expectations Drives for Results — developing level; maintaining productivity standards while meeting daily operational targets Operational Health and Safety Management — developing level; following safety guidelines to protect yourself and your team Problem Solving — foundational level; addressing routine issues that arise during daily warehouse tasks Warehouse Management — foundational level; supporting inventory control and order preparation activities What qualifications will make you successful? Strong attention to detail with a focus on accuracy and quality Team-oriented mindset and clear communication skills Eagerness to learn and grow in a dynamic warehouse environment Ability to perform physical tasks safely and efficiently throughout your shift What''s in it for me? A team culture built on safety, respect, and collaboration Training and development to help you succeed and advance your career Opportunities for growth within warehouse operations and the broader supply chain Consistent schedule with a focus on supporting your well-being Ready to start a rewarding career with a team that values your contribution? Apply now! At Schneider, we believe that every employee is a talent who deserves equal opportunities. This means you matter. Every individual needs to feel valued, supported, and treated fairly to do their best work. Our Total Rewards is our way of saying: “We see you. We value you”. It’s more than just pay and benefits- it’s a meaningful investment in you. It is designed for you to perform, grow, feel safe, and elevate your potential to shine as an impact maker. For this U.S. based position, the expected pay range is USD 0 per year. This pay range includes base pay and short-term incentives. The compensation range for this full-time position applies to candidates located within the United States. Our pay ranges are determined by reviewing roles of similar responsibility and level. Within the pay range, individual pay is determined by several factors including performance, knowledge, job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Schneider Electric is there when it matters most to you Our Total Rewards package outlines all the benefits and support you’ll enjoy as part of the Schneider Electric team: Care for Yourself and Your Family. We ensure you feel secure with benefits that help you and your family thrive: medical (with member reward points), dental, vision, and basic life insurance, Benefit Bucks, flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, well-being programs, 12 holidays per year, and 15 days of paid time off per year. Invest and Plan Your Future. We help you plan and invest for the future with competitive pay and programs including base salary, incentives, company share ownership, and 401(k) with match. Grow Your Skills and Career. We support development through performance discussions, global opportunities, the Schneider Career Hub, and learning platforms like Coursera. Team Up in the Workplace. We encourage collaboration, recognition, sharing your voice, and an inclusive workplace. Support Your Community. We make a difference through volunteer leave, programs with the Schneider Electric Foundation, youth education initiatives, and military leave benefits. Looking to make an IMPACT with your career? When you are thinking about joining a new team, culture matters. At Schneider Electric, our values and behaviors are the foundation for creating a great culture to support business success. We believe that our IMPACT values – Inclusion, Mastery, Purpose, Action, Curiosity, Teamwork – starts with us. IMPACT is also your invitation to join Schneider Electric where you can contribute to turning sustainability ambition into actions, no matter what role you play. It is a call to connect your career with the ambition of achieving a more resilient, efficient, and sustainable world. We are looking for IMPACT Makers; exceptional people who turn sustainability ambitions into actions at the intersection of automation, electrification, and digitization. We celebrate IMPACT Makers and believe everyone has the potential to be one. Become an IMPACT Maker with Schneider Electric – apply today! €40 billion global revenue +9% organic growth 150 000+ employees in 100+ countries You must submit an online application to be considered for any position with us. This position will be posted until filled. Schneider Electric aspires to be the most inclusive and caring company in the world, by providing equitable opportunities to everyone, everywhere, and ensuring all employees feel uniquely valued and safe to contribute their best. We mirror the diversity of the communities in which we operate, and ‘inclusion’ is one of our core values. We believe our differences make us stronger as a company and as individuals and we are committed to championing inclusivity in everything we do. At Schneider Electric, we uphold the highest standards of ethics and compliance, and we believe that trust is a foundational value. Our Trust Charter is our Code of Conduct and demonstrates our commitment to ethics, safety, sustainability, quality and cybersecurity, underpinning every aspect of our business and our willingness to behave and respond respectfully and in good faith to all our stakeholders. You can find out more about our Trust Charter here Schneider Electric is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is our policy to provide equal employment and advancement opportunities in the areas of recruiting, hiring, training, transferring, and promoting all qualified individuals regardless of race, religion, color, gender, disability, national origin, ancestry, age, military status, sexual orientation, marital status, or any other legally protected characteristic or conduct.', NULL, 'What''s in it for me? A team culture built on safety, respect, and collaboration Training and development to help you succeed and advance your career Opportunities for growth within warehouse operations and the broader supply chain Consistent schedule with a focus on supporting your well-being Ready to start a rewarding career with a team that values your contribution? Apply now!', 'Join our warehouse team and become part of a supply chain that delivers results every day. We''re hiring a Warehouse Operations Operator who''s ready to roll up their sleeves, work safely, and help us fulfill orders with accuracy and efficiency. What will you do? Handle receiving, storing, and shipping tasks to ensure timely and accurate order fulfillment Organize and maintain inventory while supporting proper stock rotation and product quality Operate warehouse equipment safely and follow all operational and safety procedures Collaborate with team members to meet daily productivity goals and maintain a clean, efficient workspace What are the key skills we are looking for? Continuous Improvement — developing level; identifying opportunities to streamline warehouse processes and reduce inefficiencies Customer Orientation — developing level; ensuring orders are fulfilled accurately and on time to meet customer expectations Drives for Results — developing level; maintaining productivity standards while meeting daily operational targets Operational Health and Safety Management — developing level; following safety guidelines to protect yourself and your team Problem Solving — foundational level; addressing routine issues that arise during daily warehouse tasks Warehouse Management — foundational level; supporting inventory control and order preparation activities What qualifications will make you successful? Strong attention to detail with a focus on accuracy and quality Team-oriented mindset and clear communication skills Eagerness to learn and grow in a dynamic warehouse environment Ability to perform physical tasks safely and efficiently throughout your shift', NULL, '4d53cfaa-bb9f-4ea6-9dcf-ee9e6aaeab9a', 'Fairfield', 'OH', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, 'Experienced', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-09', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', 'https://careers.se.com/jobs/121253', 'schneider_electric', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00'),
	('f90cc900-a150-4df5-aeca-bd98decd59f9', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Field Service Technician - Cooling', 'Great people make Schneider Electric a great company. Schneider’s Field Service Representatives play an impactful role within the organization - collaborating with customers, team members and third-party partners to perform assembly, startup, diagnostic, repair and preventive maintenance on both Company and third-party manufactured equipment in a variety of dynamic environments. They are problem solvers. They are customer focused. They are passionate about the work they do. They are the future of Schneider Electric! Is this you? This field service representative position will be within our U.S. Services business, specifically our Secure Power team. Our Secure Power team focuses on servicing critical data center equipment. We are the OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) service provider for APC (American Power Conversion)/Schneider Electric equipment. As a Field Service Representative, a typical day for you might include: Pre-site, startup, repair, preventive maintenance, and field modification of equipment Problem solving with customers, electricians, sales partners, technical support, District Service Completion of field service reports, expense reports, preventive maintenance, and startup data sheets Manager and/or Regional Service Director to resolve complex escalated issues Continuous learning and training on various products both in the field and in the classroom On some days, you may even: Travel throughout the region for local customer support or even countrywide travel Assist the Field Project Manager on larger system startups Act on behalf of the District Service Manager to resolve operational issues as required This may be the next step in your career journey if you have: An Associate degree, vocational education, or similar experience in HVAC/R, electronic or electrical discipline or military training equivalence 2+ years of field service repair and customer service with UPS, electrical, electro-mechanical or electronics related equipment 2+ years in Field Services or equivalent industry experience. EPA Universal Certification Safe driving and vehicle operations skills Skilled at utilizing test and diagnostic equipment Experience reading and interpreting schematics, drawings, and theory of operation manuals Ability to write service reports, correspondence, procedures, effectively present information and respond to customer questions. Movement of service equipment weighing up to 50 pounds What we have for you: Within your first 90 days, you’ll experience a unique, team-oriented welcome with 2 weeks of in-person training in our brand-new state-of-the-art training facility in Dallas, TX with all expenses paid. Upon return form your on-site visit, you’ll continue with online training and will be paired with a local area mentor to receive on-the-job training and continue your onboarding journey with us. Hear from one of our Field Service Representatives who loves her job and working with her customers! https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CAKJVzjVMTA Schneider Electric offers an inclusive benefits package to support all of our employees such as flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, 401(k) + match, well-being programs, holidays & paid time off, military leave benefits, and more. Learn more about working with us: http://se.com/us/careers Let us learn about you! Apply today. You must submit an online application to be considered for any position with us. This position will be posted until filled. Looking to make an IMPACT with your career? When you are thinking about joining a new team, culture matters. At Schneider Electric, our values and behaviors are the foundation for creating a great culture to support business success. We believe that our IMPACT values – Inclusion, Mastery, Purpose, Action, Curiosity, Teamwork – starts with us. IMPACT is also your invitation to join Schneider Electric where you can contribute to turning sustainability ambition into actions, no matter what role you play. It is a call to connect your career with the ambition of achieving a more resilient, efficient, and sustainable world. We are looking for IMPACT Makers; exceptional people who turn sustainability ambitions into actions at the intersection of automation, electrification, and digitization. We celebrate IMPACT Makers and believe everyone has the potential to be one. Become an IMPACT Maker with Schneider Electric – apply today! €40 billion global revenue +9% organic growth 150 000+ employees in 100+ countries You must submit an online application to be considered for any position with us. This position will be posted until filled. Schneider Electric aspires to be the most inclusive and caring company in the world, by providing equitable opportunities to everyone, everywhere, and ensuring all employees feel uniquely valued and safe to contribute their best. We mirror the diversity of the communities in which we operate, and ‘inclusion’ is one of our core values. We believe our differences make us stronger as a company and as individuals and we are committed to championing inclusivity in everything we do. At Schneider Electric, we uphold the highest standards of ethics and compliance, and we believe that trust is a foundational value. Our Trust Charter is our Code of Conduct and demonstrates our commitment to ethics, safety, sustainability, quality and cybersecurity, underpinning every aspect of our business and our willingness to behave and respond respectfully and in good faith to all our stakeholders. You can find out more about our Trust Charter here Schneider Electric is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is our policy to provide equal employment and advancement opportunities in the areas of recruiting, hiring, training, transferring, and promoting all qualified individuals regardless of race, religion, color, gender, disability, national origin, ancestry, age, military status, sexual orientation, marital status, or any other legally protected characteristic or conduct.', NULL, 'This may be the next step in your career journey if you have: An Associate degree, vocational education, or similar experience in HVAC/R, electronic or electrical discipline or military training equivalence 2+ years of field service repair and customer service with UPS, electrical, electro-mechanical or electronics related equipment 2+ years in Field Services or equivalent industry experience. EPA Universal Certification Safe driving and vehicle operations skills Skilled at utilizing test and diagnostic equipment Experience reading and interpreting schematics, drawings, and theory of operation manuals Ability to write service reports, correspondence, procedures, effectively present information and respond to customer questions. Movement of service equipment weighing up to 50 pounds What we have for you: Within your first 90 days, you’ll experience a unique, team-oriented welcome with 2 weeks of in-person training in our brand-new state-of-the-art training facility in Dallas, TX with all expenses paid. Upon return form your on-site visit, you’ll continue with online training and will be paired with a local area mentor to receive on-the-job training and continue your onboarding journey with us. Hear from one of our Field Service Representatives who loves her job and working with her customers! https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CAKJVzjVMTA Schneider Electric offers an inclusive benefits package to support all of our employees such as flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, 401(k) + match, well-being programs, holidays & paid time off, military leave benefits, and more. Learn more about working with us: http://se.com/us/careers Let us learn about you! Apply today. You must submit an online application to be considered for any position with us. This position will be posted until filled.', 'Great people make Schneider Electric a great company. Schneider’s Field Service Representatives play an impactful role within the organization - collaborating with customers, team members and third-party partners to perform assembly, startup, diagnostic, repair and preventive maintenance on both Company and third-party manufactured equipment in a variety of dynamic environments. They are problem solvers. They are customer focused. They are passionate about the work they do. They are the future of Schneider Electric! Is this you? This field service representative position will be within our U.S. Services business, specifically our Secure Power team. Our Secure Power team focuses on servicing critical data center equipment. We are the OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) service provider for APC (American Power Conversion)/Schneider Electric equipment. As a Field Service Representative, a typical day for you might include: Pre-site, startup, repair, preventive maintenance, and field modification of equipment Problem solving with customers, electricians, sales partners, technical support, District Service Completion of field service reports, expense reports, preventive maintenance, and startup data sheets Manager and/or Regional Service Director to resolve complex escalated issues Continuous learning and training on various products both in the field and in the classroom On some days, you may even: Travel throughout the region for local customer support or even countrywide travel Assist the Field Project Manager on larger system startups Act on behalf of the District Service Manager to resolve operational issues as required', NULL, 'dc71231e-65fc-4755-ae1f-e46d1abaf47d', 'Las Vegas', 'NV', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, 'Experienced', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-05-06', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', 'https://careers.se.com/jobs/116268', 'schneider_electric', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00'),
	('cc8866c0-fd8c-4ec4-8c76-6d222ef7b305', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Quality Inspector', 'Join Schneider Electric as a Manufacturing Process Quality Operator and help us deliver products that meet the highest standards of safety and quality. This hands-on role is perfect for someone who values precision, teamwork, and making a tangible impact on customer satisfaction. What will you do? Perform quality inspections and process control activities throughout the manufacturing process Support continuous improvement efforts that strengthen product quality and reduce risks Work with suppliers and procurement teams to resolve quality issues and implement corrective actions Ensure quality compliance during new manufacturing line setups and process changes What are the key skills we are looking for? Quality Control & Inspection — developing level; performing inspections to ensure products meet safety and quality standards Quality in Manufacturing and Distribution — developing level; applying quality processes across production and distribution operations Continuous Improvement — developing level; identifying opportunities to enhance process efficiency and reduce defects Problem Solving — developing level; analyzing quality issues and implementing practical solutions Collaboration — developing level; working with cross-functional teams to resolve quality concerns Customer Orientation — developing level; maintaining focus on delivering quality that meets customer expectations Coaching — developing level; supporting team members in understanding and applying quality standards Stakeholder Management — foundational level; coordinating with suppliers and internal partners on quality matters What qualifications will make you successful? Strong attention to detail and a commitment to upholding quality standards in every task Ability to work within established guidelines while proactively identifying improvement opportunities Effective communication skills to collaborate across teams and address quality concerns Comfortable in a dynamic manufacturing environment handling both routine and unexpected challenges New hires will begin with a Monday through Friday training schedule. After successful completion of the training period, employees will move to their designated shift assignment: 1st Shift: 6:00 AM – 4:30 PM 2nd Shift: 6:00 PM – 4:30 AM Regular schedules will be Monday through Thursday. What''s in it for me? Join a global leader committed to sustainability, innovation, and customer excellence Develop your skills through on-the-job training and continuous learning opportunities Work in a supportive team environment where quality and safety are top priorities Make a real difference by ensuring every product meets the standards our customers trust Ready to build a career where quality matters? Apply now and become part of our team! At Schneider, we believe that every employee is a talent who deserves equal opportunities. This means you matter. Every individual needs to feel valued, supported, and treated fairly to do their best work. Our Total Rewards is our way of saying: “We see you. We value you”. It’s more than just pay and benefits- it’s a meaningful investment in you. It is designed for you to perform, grow, feel safe, and elevate your potential to shine as an impact maker. For this U.S. based position, the expected pay range is USD $23-$25 per hour. This pay range includes base pay and short-term incentives. The compensation range for this full-time position applies to candidates located within the United States. Our pay ranges are determined by reviewing roles of similar responsibility and level. Within the pay range, individual pay is determined by several factors including performance, knowledge, job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Schneider Electric is there when it matters most to you Our Total Rewards package outlines all the benefits and support you’ll enjoy as part of the Schneider Electric team: Care for Yourself and Your Family. We ensure you feel secure with benefits that help you and your family thrive: medical (with member reward points), dental, vision, and basic life insurance, Benefit Bucks, flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, well-being programs, 12 holidays per year, and 15 days of paid time off per year. Invest and Plan Your Future. We help you plan and invest for the future with competitive pay and programs including base salary, incentives, company share ownership, and 401(k) with match. Grow Your Skills and Career. We support development through performance discussions, global opportunities, the Schneider Career Hub, and learning platforms like Coursera. Team Up in the Workplace. We encourage collaboration, recognition, sharing your voice, and an inclusive workplace. Support Your Community. We make a difference through volunteer leave, programs with the Schneider Electric Foundation, youth education initiatives, and military leave benefits. Looking to make an IMPACT with your career? When you are thinking about joining a new team, culture matters. At Schneider Electric, our values and behaviors are the foundation for creating a great culture to support business success. We believe that our IMPACT values – Inclusion, Mastery, Purpose, Action, Curiosity, Teamwork – starts with us. IMPACT is also your invitation to join Schneider Electric where you can contribute to turning sustainability ambition into actions, no matter what role you play. It is a call to connect your career with the ambition of achieving a more resilient, efficient, and sustainable world. We are looking for IMPACT Makers; exceptional people who turn sustainability ambitions into actions at the intersection of automation, electrification, and digitization. We celebrate IMPACT Makers and believe everyone has the potential to be one. Become an IMPACT Maker with Schneider Electric – apply today! €40 billion global revenue +9% organic growth 150 000+ employe