 supporting basic automated processes within the manual cell Customer Orientation — developing level; ensuring product quality meets customer expectations Digital Literacy — developing level; using digital tools and systems to track production data Drives for Results — developing level; meeting daily production goals with consistency and focus Lean Methodology — foundational level; applying basic lean principles to reduce waste and improve workflow Problem Solving — developing level; identifying issues and escalating them effectively to minimize downtime Quality Control & Inspection — developing level; inspecting products to ensure they meet quality standards What qualifications will make you successful? Strong attention to detail and commitment to producing high-quality work Team-oriented mindset with the ability to collaborate effectively in a production environment Reliable and accountable with a focus on meeting production targets Willingness to follow safety protocols and maintain a secure workspace', NULL, '9abcbdd3-8991-46e4-9024-97e25045a8f9', 'Cedar Rapids', 'IA', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, 'Experienced', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-16', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', 'https://careers.se.com/jobs/123389', 'schneider_electric', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00'),
	('4c71636d-0b48-4567-8a69-aa123d15c822', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Warehouse Operator', 'Join our warehouse team and become part of a supply chain that delivers results every day. We''re hiring a Warehouse Operations Operator who''s ready to roll up their sleeves, work safely, and help us fulfill orders with accuracy and efficiency. What will you do? Handle receiving, storing, and shipping tasks to ensure timely and accurate order fulfillment Organize and maintain inventory while supporting proper stock rotation and product quality Operate warehouse equipment safely and follow all operational and safety procedures Collaborate with team members to meet daily productivity goals and maintain a clean, efficient workspace What are the key skills we are looking for? Continuous Improvement — developing level; identifying opportunities to streamline warehouse processes and reduce inefficiencies Customer Orientation — developing level; ensuring orders are fulfilled accurately and on time to meet customer expectations Drives for Results — developing level; maintaining productivity standards while meeting daily operational targets Operational Health and Safety Management — developing level; following safety guidelines to protect yourself and your team Problem Solving — foundational level; addressing routine issues that arise during daily warehouse tasks Warehouse Management — foundational level; supporting inventory control and order preparation activities What qualifications will make you successful? Strong attention to detail with a focus on accuracy and quality Team-oriented mindset and clear communication skills Eagerness to learn and grow in a dynamic warehouse environment Ability to perform physical tasks safely and efficiently throughout your shift What''s in it for me? A team culture built on safety, respect, and collaboration Training and development to help you succeed and advance your career Opportunities for growth within warehouse operations and the broader supply chain Consistent schedule with a focus on supporting your well-being Ready to start a rewarding career with a team that values your contribution? Apply now! At Schneider, we believe that every employee is a talent who deserves equal opportunities. This means you matter. Every individual needs to feel valued, supported, and treated fairly to do their best work. Our Total Rewards is our way of saying: “We see you. We value you”. It’s more than just pay and benefits- it’s a meaningful investment in you. It is designed for you to perform, grow, feel safe, and elevate your potential to shine as an impact maker. For this U.S. based position, the expected pay range is USD 0 per year. This pay range includes base pay and short-term incentives. The compensation range for this full-time position applies to candidates located within the United States. Our pay ranges are determined by reviewing roles of similar responsibility and level. Within the pay range, individual pay is determined by several factors including performance, knowledge, job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Schneider Electric is there when it matters most to you Our Total Rewards package outlines all the benefits and support you’ll enjoy as part of the Schneider Electric team: Care for Yourself and Your Family. We ensure you feel secure with benefits that help you and your family thrive: medical (with member reward points), dental, vision, and basic life insurance, Benefit Bucks, flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, well-being programs, 12 holidays per year, and 15 days of paid time off per year. Invest and Plan Your Future. We help you plan and invest for the future with competitive pay and programs including base salary, incentives, company share ownership, and 401(k) with match. Grow Your Skills and Career. We support development through performance discussions, global opportunities, the Schneider Career Hub, and learning platforms like Coursera. Team Up in the Workplace. We encourage collaboration, recognition, sharing your voice, and an inclusive workplace. Support Your Community. We make a difference through volunteer leave, programs with the Schneider Electric Foundation, youth education initiatives, and military leave benefits. Looking to make an IMPACT with your career? When you are thinking about joining a new team, culture matters. At Schneider Electric, our values and behaviors are the foundation for creating a great culture to support business success. We believe that our IMPACT values – Inclusion, Mastery, Purpose, Action, Curiosity, Teamwork – starts with us. IMPACT is also your invitation to join Schneider Electric where you can contribute to turning sustainability ambition into actions, no matter what role you play. It is a call to connect your career with the ambition of achieving a more resilient, efficient, and sustainable world. We are looking for IMPACT Makers; exceptional people who turn sustainability ambitions into actions at the intersection of automation, electrification, and digitization. We celebrate IMPACT Makers and believe everyone has the potential to be one. Become an IMPACT Maker with Schneider Electric – apply today! €40 billion global revenue +9% organic growth 150 000+ employees in 100+ countries You must submit an online application to be considered for any position with us. This position will be posted until filled. Schneider Electric aspires to be the most inclusive and caring company in the world, by providing equitable opportunities to everyone, everywhere, and ensuring all employees feel uniquely valued and safe to contribute their best. We mirror the diversity of the communities in which we operate, and ‘inclusion’ is one of our core values. We believe our differences make us stronger as a company and as individuals and we are committed to championing inclusivity in everything we do. At Schneider Electric, we uphold the highest standards of ethics and compliance, and we believe that trust is a foundational value. Our Trust Charter is our Code of Conduct and demonstrates our commitment to ethics, safety, sustainability, quality and cybersecurity, underpinning every aspect of our business and our willingness to behave and respond respectfully and in good faith to all our stakeholders. You can find out more about our Trust Charter here Schneider Electric is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is our policy to provide equal employment and advancement opportunities in the areas of recruiting, hiring, training, transferring, and promoting all qualified individuals regardless of race, religion, color, gender, disability, national origin, ancestry, age, military status, sexual orientation, marital status, or any other legally protected characteristic or conduct.', NULL, 'What''s in it for me? A team culture built on safety, respect, and collaboration Training and development to help you succeed and advance your career Opportunities for growth within warehouse operations and the broader supply chain Consistent schedule with a focus on supporting your well-being Ready to start a rewarding career with a team that values your contribution? Apply now!', 'Join our warehouse team and become part of a supply chain that delivers results every day. We''re hiring a Warehouse Operations Operator who''s ready to roll up their sleeves, work safely, and help us fulfill orders with accuracy and efficiency. What will you do? Handle receiving, storing, and shipping tasks to ensure timely and accurate order fulfillment Organize and maintain inventory while supporting proper stock rotation and product quality Operate warehouse equipment safely and follow all operational and safety procedures Collaborate with team members to meet daily productivity goals and maintain a clean, efficient workspace What are the key skills we are looking for? Continuous Improvement — developing level; identifying opportunities to streamline warehouse processes and reduce inefficiencies Customer Orientation — developing level; ensuring orders are fulfilled accurately and on time to meet customer expectations Drives for Results — developing level; maintaining productivity standards while meeting daily operational targets Operational Health and Safety Management — developing level; following safety guidelines to protect yourself and your team Problem Solving — foundational level; addressing routine issues that arise during daily warehouse tasks Warehouse Management — foundational level; supporting inventory control and order preparation activities What qualifications will make you successful? Strong attention to detail with a focus on accuracy and quality Team-oriented mindset and clear communication skills Eagerness to learn and grow in a dynamic warehouse environment Ability to perform physical tasks safely and efficiently throughout your shift', NULL, '4d53cfaa-bb9f-4ea6-9dcf-ee9e6aaeab9a', 'Columbia', 'MO', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, 'Experienced', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-06-10', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', 'https://careers.se.com/jobs/123103', 'schneider_electric', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00'),
	('7cc7a138-9a3b-4c21-aac3-92cc5bb50efd', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Field Service Technician I', 'For this U.S. based position, the expected compensation range is $51,200 - $76,800 per year, which includes base pay and short-term incentive. The compensation range for this full-time position applies to candidates located within the United States. Our salary ranges are determined by reviewing roles of similar responsibility and level. Within the salary range, individual pay is determined by several factors including performance, knowledge, job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Schneider Electric also offers a comprehensive benefits package to support our employees, inclusive of medical (with member reward points), dental, vision, and basic life insurance, Benefit Bucks (credits to apply towards your benefits) flexible work arrangements, paid family leaves, 401(k) + match, well-being and recognition (including service anniversary) programs, 12 holidays per year, 15 days of paid time off per year (pro-rated in the first year of employment based on start date), opportunity to purchase company stock (eligibility depends on start date), and military leave benefits. You must submit an online application to be considered for the position. The Company will accept applications on an ongoing basis until the position is filled. Field Service Specialist What will you do? Responsible for providing high quality experience per specifications, standards, budgets and schedules, as well as participating on a team installing and servicing building automation systems Assist in reviewing contract documentation, sequences of operations, and commissioning documents Manage communications with customers, subcontractors, engineers, and project managers efficiently Participate in basic field startup using standard start up and checkout processes Assist in job close-out by providing final record drawings and documentation Responsible for all customer 