	('12ff899c-eba8-4e35-93f0-6fa10d945159', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Fabrication Associate II', 'Fabrication Associate II POSITION SUMMARY:  This position is responsible for the forming, cutting, sharpening, piercing, welding, and/or painting of fabricated materials for the use of a final product. SKILL (Education, Experience, Initiative and Ingenuity) Must be able to take and successfully pass an appropriate Work Keys assessment 1-2 years’ experience in area assigned to (Painting, Welding, Fabrication) Ability to read and understand blueprints Ability to work independently Good understanding of basic shop math and measuring techniques Expertise with basic hand tools, air tools, gages and torque wrenches Expertise in using hoist and cranes EFFORT (Physical Demand, Mental or Visual Demand) Must have excellent natural or corrected vision Job cannot be performed alternating sitting and standing Requires ability to reach overhead, lift up to 26 pounds repeatedly, be on feet for long hours, stooping, bending, pulling and pushing Must be capable of working independently using initiative and problems solving skills RESPONSIBILITY (Equipment or Process, Material or Product, Safety of Others, Work of Others) Responsible for own product quality, proper measuring techniques, and tool use and care Evaluates and performs basic troubleshooting, and obtains support from supervision, and engineering as needed May periodically provide input to supervision, engineering, and quality groups relative to product improvement Establishes and maintains a safe and healthful working environment in accordance with OSHA requirements Performs other tasks as may be requested to assure the effective and continuous utilization of assets Read and understand moderately complex blueprints, wiring diagrams, bill of materials, and schematics Chemicals: In support and coordination with EHS and Manager, performs testing and monitoring different chemical components and properties of paint line water tanks (alkalinity, pressure, temperature) In support and coordination with EHS and Manager, Responsible for replenishment and maintenance of chemicals and materials of the area In support and coordination with EHS and Manager, Responsible of water treatment and disposal system In support and coordination with EHS and Manager, coordinates safety of all employees within their area of responsibility in terms of ergonomics, chemical use, tool management, OSHA incident investigations and be a key part of the improvement process for safety improvements in the area. Fabrication Shop: Forms, cuts, and pierces metal to form fabricated assembly units Performs a variety of operations to include but not limited to: Cutting, Piercing, Forming, etc. Utilizes a wide variety of hand tools, air tools, and measuring equipment Operates moderately complex to very complex fabrication machinery, using digital/electronic controls Responsible for movement of materials within the cabinet shop area Paint Booth: Operates complex to moderately complex paint spraying equipment. May be exposed to hazardous chemicals Responsible for storage and care of chemicals Mixes and prepares paint Continuously loads and unloads parts Welding: Performs moderately complex welding operations. Utilizes a variety of welding equipment, ensuring all safety measures are used. May be exposed to extreme temperatures and performs work in a confined area. Moves parts in and out of Welding area JOB CONDITIONS (Working Conditions, Hazards) May use hazardous chemicals. Safety shoes and safety glasses are required. Hearing protection is required. Other specialized safety PPE such as face mask, gloves, apron, hard hat, face shields, and safety appropriate work clothing may also be required Looking to make an IMPACT with your career? When you are thinking about joining a new team, culture matters. At Schneider Electric, our values and behaviors are the foundation for creating a great culture to support business succe