	('9d716dfd-fc73-4cce-b143-ee83c923702c', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Warehouse Operator (1st shift)', 'What will you do? Organize and manage (or control) warehousing operations, including reception, storage, order preparation and shipments according to SPS principle. Applies strict warehouse working instructions and fixed operating procedures Comply with the health, safety and environment rules throughout the sector. Identify and express to the Team Leader (LWB3) any risks regarding health, safety, quality and environment, including reporting all incidents and near misses. Apply escalation process in case of any deviation (safety, environment, quality, performance) Know the recommended gestures to perform the standard operating modes. Suggest proposals to improve the operating mode. Link various operations according to a predetermined process: receiving, warehousing, inventory management, store outlets, line procurement Perform self-controls provided in order to detect non-conformities Operate appropriately to hazards Apply the procedures defined for the MPH Use computer resources available to save the entries and exits of the store What skills and capabilities will make you successful? Required: High School Diploma or GED Qualifications that will impact success are experience in a warehouse inventory environment; Microsoft Excel; good communication skills; ability to work in a fast-paced environment; attention to detail; prior use of powered industrial trucks such as Genie lift, PIT equipment. Experience with barcode scanning systems, and Windows based computer knowledge. Prior SAP experience. Must be able to speak, read, and understand English fluently. Work Schedule: Mon. -Thurs. 5:00am - 3:30pm What''s in it for you? Full medical, dental and vision benefits, continuous learning, internal advancement career opportunities, the opportunity to be part of the launch of Schneider ECC in Made In America project. Who will you report to? Warehouse Superviso