nsures Water Spider is kept stocked at appropriate levels of inventory Performs repetitive and advanced material supply functions following detailed work direction and guidelines May operate forklift truck or hand truck for delivery or picking of parts and supplies Sorts and counts parts and supplies and logs inventory Inspects parts for damages or defects; records discrepancies or damages and notifies supervisor and/or purchasing personnel Expedites parts and uses independent judgement to resolve part shortages May trace or track lost parts and supplies Regularly interacts with production assemblers and testers May maintain department database, prepare routine reports, and file kitter records Document material movement using computer tablets Responsible for rotating KB material FIFO Material audits, turning in and documenting KB cards for replenishment Follows established departmental policies, procedures, and objectives, continuous quality improvement objectives, and safety, environmental, and/or infection control standards Document proper care in the use and maintenance of equipment and supplies; promotes continuous improvement of workplace safety and environmental practices Establishes and maintains a safe and healthful working environment in accordance with OSHA requirements Performs other tasks as may be requested to assure the effective and continuous utilization of assets JOB CONDITIONS (Working Conditions, Hazards) Safety shoes and safety glasses are required. Work is performed in a manufacturing and assembly line environment. If material handling equipment is not operated properly, injury could result to self or others.', NULL, '4d53cfaa-bb9f-4ea6-9dcf-ee9e6aaeab9a', 'El Paso', 'TX', NULL, NULL, 'US', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{}', '{}', NULL, 'Experienced', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-03-11', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', '2026-06-30 22:37:57.623142+00', 'https://careers.se.com/jobs/110459', 'schneider_electric', '2026-0