	('a1db36fa-6d5a-4cda-923a-fa0202fb0e3a', '7446fe00-d88f-4264-a00a-7d40ce4f218d', 'Fabrication Technician - 1st Shift', 'Schneider Electric is looking for a Welding Technician for 1st shift to join our dynamic team at our Mount Juliet, TN, location. You''ll be responsible for preparing, cutting, punching, and welding metal for our cutting-edge product line. What will you do? Set-up, operate and adjust all the types of equipment such as trumpf, barline, finnpower, engel roll-form, etc. Fill in for other operators in same class and area as needed. Start up and shut down the equipment. The running of the line in auto or manual. The removal and loading of rawstock into the line as required. Making ready all materials to be run and to conduct all quality test for possible defects. Sort and dispose of scrap and write scrap tickets. Work from blue prints, sketches, routings, computer, or other documents. Maintain quality and productivity standards. Inputs information into the system either at the operator control station or a PC computer (such as schedules, quality information, downtime reasons, PM information, inslipping, etc.). Operates material handling equipment and moves loads as required. Maintains equipment, counts, records, reports production, and maintenance of daily logs. Maintain equipment including daily cleaning, dusting, tightening of bolts, checking oil levels, and reporting of abnormal conditions (heat, vibration, noise, and leaks). Maintain good housekeeping and adhere to plant regulations and safety procedures. What qualifications will make you successful? High School Diploma or equivalent 2+ years MIG/Spot Welding experience required Must be a self-starter and independent worker Previous fabrication experience Previous experience at setting dies Ability to develop some computer skills Forklift experience preferred but not required Our basic requirements: The department requires PPE (Personal Protective Equipment), plus Safety shoes and safety glasses mus