liance, and we believe that trust is a foundational value. Our Trust Charter is our Code of Conduct and demonstrates our commitment to ethics, safety, sustainability, quality and cybersecurity, underpinning every aspect of our business and our willingness to behave and respond respectfully and in good faith to all our stakeholders. You can find out more about our Trust Charter here Schneider Electric is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is our policy to provide equal employment and advancement opportunities in the areas of recruiting, hiring, training, transferring, and promoting all qualified individuals regardless of race, religion, color, gender, disability, national origin, ancestry, age, military status, sexual orientation, marital status, or any other legally protected characteristic or conduct.', NULL, 'What''s in it for me? A team culture built on safety, respect, and collaboration Training and development to help you succeed and advance your career Opportunities for growth within warehouse operations and the broader supply chain Consistent schedule with a focus on supporting your well-being Ready to start a rewarding career with a team that values your contribution? Apply now!', 'Join our warehouse team and become part of a supply chain that delivers results every day. We''re hiring a Warehouse Operations Operator who''s ready to roll up their sleeves, work safely, and help us fulfill orders with accuracy and efficiency. What will you do? Handle receiving, storing, and shipping tasks to ensure timely and accurate order fulfillment Organize and maintain inventory while supporting proper stock rotation and product quality Operate warehouse equipment safely and follow all operational and safety procedures Collaborate with team members to meet daily productivity goals and maintain a clean, efficient workspace What are the key skills we are looking for? Continuous Improvement — developing level; identifying opportunities to streamline warehouse processes and red