rotating schedule', 'Working knowledge with PLC’s (e.g., Allen Bradley, RSLogix 5000, Square D, Control Logix) servo controls and variable frequency drives (e.g., Rockwell Powerflex) is required
Must be proficient in reading electrical blueprints and ladder logic prints, have knowledge of Ethernet, DH+, and RS Links/Logics
Strong computer skills
Experience in:
Industrial controls, conveyance systems, sub-stations, motor control centers, power distribution panels, electrical starters, variable frequency drives (VFDs)
Computerized maintenance management systems
Multi-disciplined fast-paced work environment where Safety, Quality, Delivery, Cost, People, Maintenance, and Environment (SQDCPME) are the focus of all organizational objectives
Troubleshooting electrical and robotic systems and equipment (e.g., Fanuc, Kawasaki, ABB, Siemens)
