	('6e78ea01-ce66-438f-a6d6-5ab830a73a18', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Machinist Technician Technology Program-1', 'GE partnered with Hudson Valley to create the Machinist Technician Technology Program (MTTP) which combines both academic studies and on-the-job training to develop the fundamentals required to become a skilled machinist with GE Power machine tools. Students will attend class at Hudson Valley 4-days a week and report to the GE Schenectady site 1-day a week for training during the fall and spring semester. Students will train full-time during a summer semester through an internship, and will be eligible for employment as a GE machinist following graduation.
Program Summary
Specialized 2-year program combining on-the-job training with coursework through Hudson Valley Technical College
Students spend 4-days a week in the classroom and 1-day onsite training during the school year
Mandatory internship during the summer term
All applicants will go through a entry exam and interview process prior to employment
Apprentices paid for on-the-job training
Tuition, and books paid by GE through sponsorship
All applicants will be subject to a retention agreement of 2 years in order to be sponsored by GE
Mentoring, teamwork, ongoing reviews
Earn a 2-year Machine Tool Technology Associates Degree
Training in basic measurements, assembly, safety, print reading, and many other manufacturing processes
Hands on experience working in a manufacturing environment
Skill set with the latest machining technology
Personal development through coaching and mentoring
Ability to make a measurable impact
Entry into an in-demand skilled craft
Essential Responsibilities
Work from drawings, sketches, and other instructions to perform machining operations such as mill, turn, face, bore, groove, contour, dovetail, drill, tap, etc. to precise mechanical tolerances
Assists in taking and recording various measurements / runouts of components
Report any conflicts to the Shift Supervisor
Complete daily point of work risk assessments and Safety Observations
Record and report daily time
Aggressively maintain a safe working environment to include good housekeeping practices of assigned work area and comply with all applicable environmental, health and safety policies
Perform tooling set-up and maintenance activities as directed
Maintain classroom GPA of B or better
Pass technical ability reviews during summer internship period
Qualifications/Requirements
High School Diploma / GED
1 – year work experience or education in machining specific trade area
ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS:
Ability to score at least a 75% on entry exam
Ability, with or without accommodation, to pass site functional test lift/push/pull
Ability and willingness to work overtime as required
Ability and willingness to work occasional weekend shifts
Ability and willingness to work on an off-shift (2nd: 3pm-11pm, 3rd: 11pm-7am)
Ability and willingness to wear personal protective equipment, for example safety glasses, gloves, ear plugs, and safety shoes
Ability and willingness to take a pre-employment test and submit to technical interview to maintain program sponsorship
Legal authorization to work in the U.S. is required. We will not sponsor individuals for employment visas, now or in the future, for this job.
Employment is contingent on applicant signing a 2-year retention agreement with GE that begins after program graduation.
Desired Characteristics:
Able to read blueprints
Strong math skills
Able to use, read, and understand measuring tools
Knowledge of common PC tools, Excel, Word, Power Point, etc
Reading comprehension; understanding written sentences and paragraphs in work related documents
Able to follow written instructions and take verbal instructions
Able to work with computerized shop floor tools to include, but not limited to: vouchering systems, on-line quality programs, and payroll management tools
Ability to work alone or as part of a team with minimal supervision
The pay for this position is $28.01 per hour
.  This position is also eligible for shift premium when you work on an off shift i.e. 2nd or 3rd shift. Plus $1.00 USD an hour on top of base pay.
