	('f11f0594-c133-449f-9895-24f2911fbf4c', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Electrician', 'The Operation Support A - Electrician will install, repair, and maintain all electrical and Facilities mechanical systems and equipment. In this role you will drive cycle time improvements, EHS actions, and design and implement necessary fixtures and tooling for manufacturing improvements.
In addition, you will:
Troubleshoot & repair equipment and building electrical systems. Maintain and repair electrical components such as motors, transformers, switch gear, rectifiers, control systems, fire alarms, motor control centers, and shop machinery power feeds.
Run conduit, replace fuses, make new electrical gear installations, troubleshoot circuitry.
Perform office electrical maintenance, light trimming, & new installations.
Work with schematics and wiring diagrams, order material.
Make comprehensive inspection using a variety of inspection instruments and gauges to detect malfunctions
Analyze and diagnose cause of malfunctions, failures, and repetitive manufacturing problems and recommend and implement proper corrective actions
Analyze malfunctions and execute the repair of control systems and install, maintain, or modify such systems
Perform facilities and equipment maintenance, as needed
Plan, layout, rig, move, erect, and install complex equipment and machinery, overhead cranes, etc.
Keep work areas and equipment clean and operating safely
Train others, as necessary
Participate in and own Environmental, Health, and Safety (EHS) initiatives and performance throughout the plant
Identify and implement process improvement opportunities to improve quality and product flow
Participate in lean initiatives, using 6 Sigma tools for process improvements
Identify and implement Kaizens for continuous improvement
undefined
