	('fea752b1-e9c3-495f-bd73-b0e4780eeb98', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Toolmaker', 'We are looking for an Entry Level Toolmaker to join our team. This position is ideal for individuals who are passionate about precision manufacturing and eager to learn hands-on skills in tooling fabrication, fixture maintenance, and prototyping. The primary focus of this role is to assist in maintaining the health of production fixtures, support prototype development, and work alongside experienced tool makers to gain valuable experience in the manufacturing environment. Included in this scope is the ability to ensure cleanliness of fixtures prior to and performing the preventative maintenance.
The primary responsibility of this role will be focusing on the cleanliness and Preventative Maintenance of fixtures (replacing critical components such as bolts/dowel pins/locators/and other wear components). With time permitting, the employee shall be focusing on their development as a tool maker working alongside the tool makers of 20+ years experience.
Essential Functions/Responsibilities:
Clean fixtures
in the designated area with provided methods, utilizing the correct PPE
Perform
preventative maintenance
of production fixtures to ensure operational efficiency.
Learn and support basic fixture repair and assembly under the guidance of experienced tool makers.
Conduct repairs in the tool room to ensure operational efficiency and reliability of tooling and fixtures.
Support prototype development by assisting in the fabrication and modification of fixtures, jigs, and other tooling components.
Gain hands-on experience operating machine tools such as lathes, mills, grinders, lasers and CNC machines.
Assist in measuring and verifying machined components to ensure accuracy and conformance to specifications.
Read and interpret technical drawings, blueprints, and work instructions.
Work within tight tolerances to ensure high precision in tooling components.
Verify dimensions, alignments, and clearances using measuring instruments such as dial indicators, gauge blocks, thickness gauges, and micrometers.
Work collaboratively with engineers, designers, and senior tool makers to develop and refine tooling solutions.
Actively contribute to Lean Kaizen events aimed at improving the efficiency and effectiveness of production fixtures and processes.
Maintain a clean and organized workspace, adhering to all safety and quality standards.
Report any unusual problems or conditions to the supervisor.
Perform additional duties as assigned.
Minimum Eligibility Requirements:
Ability to work 1st Shift (6:30am-2:30pm)
High School Diploma or GED equivalent
Minimum of 2 years’ experience in EDM/CNC, tooling production or equivalent, or technical degree in Tool & Die Making
Legal authorization to work in the U.S. is required
Basic mechanical skills
Proficient shop math skills
Basic computer skills, Microsoft Word & Excel.
Ability to lift/push/pull at least 50 pounds, with or without reasonable accommodation
Ability to work overtime as required, including weekends
Capable of simple assembly & fabrication
Willingness to wear personal protective equipment, for example: safety glasses, gloves, ear plugs, and safety shoes
Knowledge of machine tool geometry and problem-solving skills to ensure equipment is functioning properly
This role requires use of technical data subject to U.S. Government export restrictions and this posting is only for U.S. Persons (U.S. Citizens, lawful permanent residents and protected individuals (e.g., certain refugees and asylees)). GE will require proof of status prior to employment.
​
Desired Characteristics:
Experience in manufacturing, tooling production, or equivalent
Demonstrates positive attitude, strong work ethic, and self-motivation
Strong desire to learn the toolmaker trade & be mentored by experienced tool makers.
Ability to be a strong team player and flexible to move to different areas as required
Ability to follow verbal & written instructions for multiple assembly tasks in a manufacturing shop environment
Ability to work alone or as part of a team with minimal supervision
Read Technical Drawings/Blueprints
Experience using Knee Mills (Bridgeport), Lathes, Surface Grinders, Hydraulic Press, Hand Tools a plus
Ability to read and interpret M&G code a plus
Interest in developing a long-term career in Tool & Die Making and precision machining at Metem, a GE Vernova business
The pay for this position is $29.50/hr. to $36.88/hr. This posting is expected to remain open and close when a suitable candidate is identified.
If you are a motivated individual looking to work in a dynamic environment with opportunities for skill development and process improvements, we encourage you to apply to be part of the Toolmaking team.
