	('87039035-2e2c-4ac4-88dc-622257fe982d', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Senior Wind Technician - Travel (US)', 'The Senior Wind Technician – Travel is a critical and active role to maintain optimal function and output at the wind site by working daily on turbine operations, required maintenance, safety, quality control and warranty repair(s). The Senior Wind Technician – Travel partners and communicates with the Resource Manager and Site Leadership to execute on contract requirements and timelines and ensures alignment with the GE Vernova Way!
Essential Responsibilities:
As the Senior Wind Technician –
Travel (United States), you will
:
Work with Resource Managers and Site Leadership to execute contractual obligations per customer requirements and activities set forth on a daily basis which include any portion of the electrical and mechanical equipment used in the GE wind turbine generators across North America.
Help in all areas of site preparation (coordination of labor and materials) with minimal supervision.
Participate in pre-job meetings to discuss schedule, weather, LOTO (Lock Out Tag Out), hazards, and jobsite / customer requirements.
Troubleshoot mechanical, hydraulic, and electrical problems on wind turbines including perform diagnostic electrical analysis.
Perform maintenance, repair, or replacement of parts to correct wind turbine malfunctions.
Document all work performed using company provided technology.
1`1`11Qualifications/Requirements:
High School Diploma or equivalent, and
Minimum of 4 years experience
as a Wind Technician and
