Troubleshooting: Diagnose and troubleshoot electrical issues, malfunctions, and failures in system. Analyze and resolve complex problems efficiently and safely.
Safety Compliance: Adhere to all safety guidelines and regulations while working with energized equipment. Ensure that safety protocols are followed by yourself and the team. This includes following all NFPA 70E electrical safety requirements.
Documentation: Maintain accurate records of maintenance activities, equipment inspections, and repairs. Keep up-to-date documentation of HVAC systems, including schematics and diagrams. Maintain required EPA records for refrigerant leaks and equipment disposals.
Emergency Response: Be on-call for emergency HVAC repairs and respond promptly to minimize downtime and safety risks.
