Ability and willingness to read and communicate in the English language.
Ability and willingness to lift 40lbs.
Desired Characteristics:
Able to read and interpret service repair manuals and technical publications to determine work procedures.
Demonstrate knowledge and skills in the use of various hand tools including but not limited to torque wrenches, transducers, multipliers, dial indicators, micrometers, scales and other precision instrumentation.
Basic computer skills.
Strong verbal, written, analytical and interpersonal skills.
Prior experience working with different types of engines / packages / Gas turbine product lines.
Experience with LM2500, LM6000, LMS100 or other Aero-derivative Gas Turbine Engines or Packages.
Borescope Inspection experience.
Familiarity with static & dynamic balancing theory and procedures.
Thorough knowledge of FOD / DOD prevention and control', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '9abcbdd3-8991-46e4-9024-97e25045a8f9', 'Houston', 'TX', NULL, NULL, 'US', 'on_site', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '$37.21 per hour', '{}', '{}', NULL, 'entry', NULL, false, false, true, '2026-05-05', 'scraper', NULL, '2026-06-30 23:00:14.519387+00', '2026-06-30 23:00:14.519387+00', 'https://careers.gevernova.com/turbine-tech-1st-shift/job/R5040083', 'ge_vernova', '2026-06-30 23:00:14.519387+00'),
	('871951c4-5cd2-4541-9f8d-0dbaa2a1d141', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Advanced Machinist X 3rd shift', 'What impact you’ll make?
The Machine Operator X will work at the Greenville, SC Gas Turbine Manufacturing plant and will work set-up and operate a variety of advanced technical/ complex production equipment and tooling in a gas turbine manufacturing facility. You will also have ownership of compliance, safety, quality, and productivity in position of responsibilities.
What You’ll Do:
• Set up and operate a wide range of advanced manual, conventional, and CNC machines to manufacture gas turbine parts and tooling of various sizes and complexities.
• Assemble and disassemble parts as needed to prepare for machining processes.
• Perform detailed machine setups, including:
– Assembling, positioning, and aligning fixtures
– Establishing coordinate systems and inputting offsets
– Measuring tools and entering dimensional data and compensation values
• Run machines safely for testing new processes, programs, and adjustments.
• Monitor and adjust equipment to ensure quality parts throughout production.
• Diagnose and resolve problems across fixtures, machines, programs, and inspections.
• Perform regular preventive maintenance and troubleshoot equipment issues.
• Maintain part quality by consistently refining and monitoring processes.
• Collaborate with engineers and programmers to improve processes and report deviations.
• Conduct inspections and quality control checks using gauges and measuring instruments.
• Actively participate in team efforts, lean initiatives, and continuous improvement efforts.
• Take on additional related tasks and responsibilities as required.
Why Join Us?
• Work at a world-class gas turbine manufacturing plant supporting global energy infrastructure.
• Access state-of-the-art machining technology and collaborate with experienced professionals.
• Grow in a role that values safety, precision, and process innovation.
• Enjoy opportunities to contribute to lean manufacturing and continuous improvement.
What You’ll Bring:
• High school diploma, GED, or equivalent
• Successful completion of the 01X Advanced Machinist Assessment
• Completion of a technical machinist or tool maker program OR at least 1 year of experience operating manual, conventional, or CNC machines such as VTLs, VBMs, HBMs, large milling machines, NC grinders, or lathes
• Ability to work 3rd shift (11PM - 7AM), including overtime and occasional weekends
• Comfortable working in a tobacco-free environment and wearing required PPE
• Capable of lifting up to 50 lbs and standing for extended periods
• Able to pass a background check and drug screening
• Legal authorization to work in the U.S. (visa sponsorship not available)', '• Technically skilled in setting up and operating complex machining equipment
• Detail-oriented with strong troubleshooting and mechanical problem-solving abilities
• Safety-conscious, quality-driven, and focused on continuous improvement
• Team-oriented with a proactive and flexible attitude toward tasks and schedules
• Comfortable working hands-on in a dynamic and fast-paced production environment
Tools & Equipment You’ll Work With:
• Manual, conventional, and CNC machines (VTL, VBM, HBM, milling machines, grinders, etc.)
• Tool measurement systems and machine control software
• Precision measuring devices (calipers, gauges, fixtures)
• Fixtures, jigs, and part setups for complex turbine components
Machine Operator X:
Pay Rate: $36.706 – $37.967 per hour
• Eligible for a $1.00/hour shift premium on 2nd or 3rd shift
• This job posting is expected to close on June 15th, 2026
