	('961ece39-70a0-479c-8e37-6afdc4347102', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Lead CNC Programmer VTL', 'Are you passionate about innovation? Are you excited at the opportunity to electrify and decarbonize the world?
We operate with a founder’s mindset. We deliver innovation with passion, speed, and courage. We continuously challenge our thinking and are empowered to dream big and take smart risks.
As a member of the CAD/CAM team, you will be an active contributor to the factory volume ramp and standardization efforts.
What you’ll do
Generate toolpath and create CNC programs utilizing Siemens NX-CAM 2412
Support large Toshulin VTL processes (up to 2.5m)
Simulate all CNC programs prior to release to the shop floor utilizing Vericut v9.6.
Incorporate on-machine probing for part and process validation (including error trapping)
Define tooling and work holding for new processes as well as optimize tooling and work holding for existing processes
Create and manage tool libraries in a TDM database
Develop new or modify existing processes to ensure safety and process security
Prove out new programs alongside machine operators and manufacturing engineers
Create programs following standards and qualified machining parameters
Provide CNC related support to M.E. (Manufacturing Engineer) and provide operator training as warranted
Provide daily operator support and problem solving to the shop
Generate and support workstation instructions (methods) for CNC related issues.
Initiate and lead process improvement projects to improve safety, quality, cost and delivery.
Provide effective communication to appropriate team members when needed.
Work effectively as an individual and in a team-based environment in a matrixed organization.
Work effectively in a fast-paced environment while embracing and driving positive change inside and outside the organization when appropriate.
What you’ll bring (Basic Qualifications)
Bachelor’s Degree, Associate’s Degree, or Machinist Apprentice (or similar) graduate with 3 years of experience with graphical based CAM System CNC Programming [OR] High School Degree w/6 years of experience with graphical based CAM System CNC Programming.
What will make you stand out
Preference will be given to candidates with Siemens NX CAM experience (1953 or later)
Extensive experience machining nickel-based superalloys (Inconel, Rene, Hastelloy, etc.) common in Heavy Duty Gas Turbine (HDGT) or Aerospace industry
Strong familiarity with multiple machine controls including Fanuc, Haas, Okuma, & Siemens
Proven experience with variable-based programming, macro routines, and advanced Renishaw probing for "closed-loop" machining and automated error-trapping.
Significant "hands-on" background as a machinist, with the ability to personally setup and prove out complex first-piece programs.
A track record of managing tight tolerances on large-format equipment (VTLs/VBMs up to 2.5m) where part deflection and thermal stability are critical factors
Bachelor degree in Engineering or Machine Tool Technology.
Strong problem solving and organization skills, with above average shop math skills in algebra, geometry, and trigonometry.
Demonstrated proficiency interpreting drawing requirements.
Ability to multi-task and productively manage multiple projects concurrently.
