	('fee7d838-fc90-42c9-81ab-04a13f6b1725', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Non-Destructive Test (NDT) Technician', 'The NDT Inspector performs non‑destructive testing on steam and gas turbine components and generator parts, supporting quality assurance in both factory and field environments.
Essential Functions/Responsibilities:
Follow all safety procedures and participate in required safety training.
Perform assigned inspections and tasks under direction of Supervisor/Leadman.
Demonstrate strong communication and work habits consistent with the Behavioral Skills section of the Skills Matrix.
Conduct NDT inspections including:
Magnetic Particle (MT):
rotors, casings, vane carriers, blades, fusion lines, hot MT
Dye Penetrant (PT):
removed/installed blades, retaining rings, faceplates, generator dovetails, vane carriers, wedges, and hardware; operate penetrant line
Ultrasonic (UT):
bearings, braze coupons, tenons, installed blade pins, weld build‑ups, phased array weld build‑ups, phased array L‑O steeples, flaw depth sizing, retaining ring forgings/bar stock; follow all UT safety requirements
Perform hardness testing using Equotip, Wilson, and Clark equipment
Prepare NCRs and complete all steps in I&T Plans.
Communicate professionally with team members and support workforce skill development
Perform other functions as assigned
Qualifications/Requirements:
Ability to work 1st shift (7-330pm) or 2nd shift (3-11:30pm)
High School diploma or GED
NT, PT, UT Level 2 Certification – with 5 years’ experience
Ability to work overtime as required, including occasional weekend shifts', NULL, 'Significant technical experience (approximately 5 or more years) with a variety of power generating equipment (steam and gas)
Strong math skills and the ability to perform complex mathematical calculations
Ability to work independently and with others under stressful conditions
Ability to follow written and verbal instructions to solve complex problem
Ability to document and follow proper procedures and train others to do so
The pay for this position is $26.00 to $41.50/hr. plus $2/hr. shift differential. For senior position, the pay is $42.50-$46/hr. plus $2hr. shift differential. This posting is expected to remain open until a suitable candidate is identified.
