	('6cb05ec9-6c02-4068-8036-a33b9aa48db1', '89f29d7c-723f-4203-9349-d81228744f3d', 'Fabrication & CAD Technician', 'The robotics team technician plays a critical hands-on role supporting the Robotics & Computer Vision team at GE Vernova Advanced Research. This position provides CAD-to-fabrication support, light machining and assembly, and day-to-day ownership of laboratory spaces and equipment.
Working closely with engineers and researchers, the Technician helps transform designs and ideas into physical prototypes by preparing CAD files for fabrication, operating and maintaining lab equipment, and contributing practical insights that improve manufacturability, usability, and reliability. This role also serves as a steward of the robotics lab environment, ensuring tools, equipment, and spaces are safe, organized, and ready to support fast-moving research and development work.
The Robotics team values collaboration, craftsmanship, and shared ownership. This is a hands-on role for someone who enjoys building, maintaining, and improving things — and who takes pride in enabling others to do their best technical work.', NULL, NULL, 'Fabrication & CAD/CAM Support
Support engineers by converting CAD designs into fabrication-ready files with expertise in and through understanding of CAM software and 3D printing slicers.
Fabricate robotic components and prototypes using CNC machines, 3D printers, and external PCB manufacturing services.
Perform light machining, assembly, and finishing of prototype components.
Lab Ownership & Equipment Maintenance
Maintain and organize robotics laboratory spaces, ensuring tools, materials, and equipment are operational and readily available.
Schedule, perform, or coordinate maintenance on lab equipment including ‘fit and finish’ metalworking equipment, 3D printers, laser cutters, and related tools.
Maintain required supplies, tooling, and consumables for fabrication activities.
Job Scheduling & Coordination
Manage a queue of fabrication/assembly and lab support requests, including scheduling, prioritization, and job logging.
Coordinate closely with engineering teams to align priorities and delivery timelines.
Technical Collaboration
Participate in technical discussions with engineers to provide input on designs for ease of fabrication, ergonomics, repairability, and operation.
Independently troubleshoot and resolve mechanical and fabrication-related issues where objectives are defined but solutions require judgment and experience.
Laboratory Operations & Safety
Maintain standard laboratory equipment and facilities, including calibration of instruments and monitoring devices.
Develop, maintain, and follow relevant Environmental, Health, and Safety (EHS) documentation and procedures.
Perform all work in accordance with GE Vernova EHS guidelines and compliance policies.
Documentation & Reporting
Document test setups, fabrication procedures, and key results or findings.
Perform basic data processing and prepare reports using tools such as Microsoft Excel and Word.
Qualifications / Requirements
Associate degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field with a focus on machining, fabrication, and mechanical design
OR
High School Diploma with a minimum of 8 years of relevant hands-on experience, with a focus on robotics, machine design, or prototyping.
Substantial experience fabricating test fixtures and prototype components for robotics or electromechanical systems.
Experience using electrical assembly tools such as crimping and soldering to support robotic prototype assembly.
Demonstrated ability to work independently, manage multiple tasks, and deliver quality work to defined objectives.
Legal authorization to work in the U.S. is required. This role is not eligible for immigration or visa sponsorship.
This position requires access to information and technology subject to U.S. export control laws; only “U.S. persons” as defined by law may be considered.
Must be willing to work on-site at GE Vernova Advanced Research in
Niskayuna, NY
.
Desired Characteristics
Familiarity with Solidworks and a CAM package, (bonus if familiarity as well with AutoCAD)
Hands-on experience with 3D printers, lathes, CNC mills, and laser cutters.
Familiarity with lab and experiment tools such as Python, G-code, LabVIEW, or similar and a willingness to learn new software packages
Strong organizational skills and a demonstrated track record of completing tasks and deliverables on schedule.
Pride in craftsmanship, lab ownership, and maintaining high standards of safety and quality.
Collaborative mindset and enjoyment of working closely with engineers and researchers.
Why Join the Robotics Team
The Robotics & Computer Vision group at GE Vernova Advanced Research is a close-knit, collaborative team that values technical excellence, mutual respect, and shared success. Technicians are treated as essential partners in the work — not just support staff — and their experience and judgment are trusted and respected.
